  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1241 AM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nSouth Texas will remain relatively dry through the week outside of \ndaily seabreeze convection paired with weak shortwaves passing \nthrough that will lead to low chances for activity. Warm \ntemperatures will remain in place until Thursday. Guidance \n(GFS,Canadian,ECMWF) has remained in agreement that a cold front is \nexpected to swing through the region at the conclusion of the week. \nThe timing will appears to be late Friday into early Saturday. One \nof the likely impacts that guidance still is hinting at is windy \nconditions especially over the waters. Small Craft Advisory \nconditions will likely be expected with the possibility for Gale \nconditions. The strength of the front still remains a bit in \nquestion. With the differences in the guidance remaining confidence \nunfortunately will remain low at this time, though we continue to \nmonitoring the trends. Things will become more clear when we are in \nrange of the higher resolution models. Although rain chances have \ndecreased a bit from previous forecast, showers and thunderstorms \nwill still be possible with the frontal passage. \n\nOtherwise, today we likely still see continued minor coastal \nflooding in the region. Still expecting a continued downtrend, \nthough noticed some spots where tides reached higher than normal. \nDecision was made to extend the Coastal Flood Advisory until early \nWednesday morning. Another extension maybe possible as PE-TSS still \nmaintains tides around 1.8 MSL. Will continue to monitor the webcams \nand guidance through the day today.",
